sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch11-18> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "The form and direction of brachiopod spiral arms (brachidia) are determined by their initial curvature and the space and pressures within the shell, so that long outwardly directed spirals should go with transversely elongated shells such as Spirifer, inwardly directed spirals with rounded shells such as Atrypa, and discoid spirals with strongly flattened shells.";
    dc:type "prediction";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Brachiopod spiral arm direction follows shell shape through spatial constraint";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter XI, “The Logarithmic Spiral”; topic “Spiral arms of Brachiopods”. Scope: spire-bearing brachiopods (Spiriferida, Atrypida, Athyridida and others)"
}
