sub:quote a prov:Entity;
    prov:hadPrimarySource <https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/55264/pg55264.txt#line=19066,19073>;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/55264>;
    <https://schema.org/text> "It is obvious that the incipient curvature of the arms, and consequently the form and direction of the spirals, will be influenced by the surrounding pressures, and these in turn by the general shape of the shell. We shall expect, accordingly, to find the long outwardly directed spirals associated with shells which are transversely elongated, as Spirifer is; while the more rounded Atrypas will tend to the opposite condition.".
